---
import Main from "../../layouts/Main.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import MediaCTA from "../../components/MediaCTA.astro";
import { IMG_LAND, BAN_FUTURES } from "../../data/media";
import { strategicFutures } from "../../data/strategic-lanes";
---

<Main
  title="Strategic Futures - SyncI&DLabs"
  description="The strategic futures SyncI&DLabs actualizes, funded through a Long-Term Fund that builds coalitions of ventures toward common futures: sovereign energy and compute, resilient neighbourhoods, food sovereignty, advanced manufacturing and Industry 4.0, Arctic sovereignty, emerging technologies and quantum computing, health, and the CITAble methodology."
  lang="en"
  activePath="/futures"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Strategic futures"
    title="The futures we actualize."
    lead="Each is a Canadian challenge we read from the ecosystems we know, then build toward. We do not forecast these futures. We work toward them, venture by venture, through coalitions across the district network."
    image={BAN_FUTURES}
    imageAlt="Aerial Canadian land at dawn"
  />

  <section class="border-b border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">The authoritative list</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-4 max-w-3xl text-2xl font-medium leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">
        Eight directions, one coalition.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        Every campus and industry district in the network works the full range. The difference is
        emphasis, not scope: research-oriented campuses lead discovery, and pre-commercialization
        campuses lead the bridge to market. The futures themselves are shared.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px bg-hairline md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          strategicFutures.map((lane) => (
            <div class="bg-canvas p-8">
              <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">{lane.name}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">{lane.line}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Long-Term Fund -->
  <section class="border-b border-hairline">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">How the futures are funded</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        The Long-Term Fund.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        A future is built by a coalition, not a single venture. The Long-Term Fund (LTF) is how the
        coalition forms: patient capital deployed against a strategic thesis, combined with
        constellation-style acquisition of keystone companies, and owner-operator stewardship that
        holds them for decades rather than growing them to sell. Companies are gathered into one
        fund per future, so they combine to actualize a common future and every member benefits
        from the greater economic returns that scale and coordination produce.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-px bg-hairline md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="bg-canvas p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">Coalition, not a single bet</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
            Ventures aligned to the same future are gathered together, so they share market share,
            infrastructure, and talent rather than competing for it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-canvas p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">Keystone acquisition</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
            We acquire and retool keystone companies, the ones that unlock a whole future, and
            steward them as permanent assets that compound.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-canvas p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink">Shared returns</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-graphite">
            Because the coalition builds one future together, the economic returns are greater than
            any member could reach alone, and they accrue back into the fund.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Canada's opportunity: the founding-thesis arc -->
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 lg:px-10">
      <p class="eyebrow text-graphite/60">Why this is worth building</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-6 text-3xl font-medium leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Canada is the opportunity.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-graphite">
        We began by reading Waterloo as a small place of outsized potential, and set out to amplify
        it with a venture-studio model rather than bet on one company. Across a decade, that
        ecosystem produced an estimated 25 to 40 billion dollars in value. We now read the whole country the same
        way. Canada holds a multi-trillion-dollar opportunity over the coming decades, spread
        across every future on this page, if it can build the coalitions to capture it at home.
        Anchor ventures already under way include DAICompute (sovereign compute), Iterra (food),
        Arcadia Wellness (health), and Nova Roma with Perceptiosphere (education and research).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm italic text-graphite/70">
        National figures are directional estimates under a coordinated sovereignty scenario. The
        verified problem statement is on <a href="/en/research" class="accent-link">The Canadian Gap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <MediaCTA
    image={IMG_LAND}
    eyebrow="Buildable, not speculative"
    headline="Foresight scenarios we actively work toward, on real land."
    ctaLabel="See the district design"
    ctaHref="/en/district"
  />
</Main>
